 deliberate restart

The conductor has run as one process since 2026-08-24 17:53:49 and therefore
holds the module copies it imported then. The gate-reload fix (82d8219adf,
2026-08-25 09:49:24) lives in scripts/research_conductor.py, which that process
loaded about 21 hours before the fix existed -- so the fix for the stale-import
problem is itself behind the stale-import problem. It becomes real only on a
restart.

Committing first rather than stashing, per the standing never-revert rule. The
conductor was mid-close on 575 writing audit output, so these five files are
in-flight state: two audit reports and three guard state files. Audit reports
regenerate at the next close; the state files should not be lost.

